id: pm-f60039
title: "GH-1143: Claude session-file provenance resolver ignores real nested stream fields"
description: GitHub issue #1143 shows 85 model and version resolver attempts with zero success even though the canonical Claude session file exists and contains message.model plus top-level version after initial metadata rows. The shipped reader appears unable to traverse the real JSONL layout.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:provenance","area:sdk",context-integrity,github-1143,harness,observability
created_at: "2026-08-28T21:26:05.521Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T23:38:19.595Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T23:26:16.232Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T23:26:16.232Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: The resolver parses a captured real-layout JSONL fixture with leading metadata and nested message.model; Scanning is byte and row bounded and never emits paths identifiers prompts or session content; Malformed and truncated rows fail closed while later complete rows remain discoverable; Model and version success counters move above zero in real-layout acceptance without additional provider calls; SDK health history CLI and exact coverage gates pass
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub issue #1143
severity: high
environment: pm 2026.8.28 with Claude Code 2.1.251 and a readable canonical session JSONL stream
repro_steps: Run pm mutations under a real Claude session whose first rows are metadata; model first appears at message.model and version on later assistant rows; observe health zero-success warnings for every attempt.
resolution: Implemented a privacy-preserving bounded Claude JSONL resolver that scans nested message metadata across head and tail windows with path-size-mtime caching.
expected_result: The bounded privacy-preserving resolver scans complete real-layout rows until it finds supported nested model and version fields and records successful probe provenance without exposing session content.
actual_result: "Real-layout nested model and version fixtures resolve successfully while malformed, deep, and oversized streams remain bounded and do not expose session content."
component: SDK agent provenance resolver and health diagnostics
customer_impact: Immutable history loses model and runtime attribution while a permanent health warning trains operators to ignore resolver failures.
